# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Applied before the asset lookup.
#
# Currently empty, and that is deliberate. Two rules that look reasonable here
# do not work on Pages, and fail *silently* — they sit in the file looking
# correct while doing nothing:
#
#   1. Host-based rules. `_redirects` matches on PATH only. A line like
#        https://www.ehsanmolaei.ir/* https://ehsanmolaei.ir/:splat 301
#      is ignored. www -> apex is therefore a dashboard Redirect Rule
#      (Rules -> Redirect Rules), which can read the hostname.
#
#   2. Query-string rules. Same problem: the query is not part of the match, so
#        /resume?variant=romania  /resume/romania/  301
#      would never fire. Those old URLs were never indexed (variant pages are
#      noindex) and were only ever used locally, so no redirect is needed.
#
# Path-only redirects DO work here, e.g.:
#   /old-page/  /new-page/  301
# Add them below as the site changes.
